description: SpryMD repository defaults for Cursor
alwaysApply: true
---

- Use Bun for package management and scripts. `bun.lock` is the source of truth and the committed `package-lock.json` is stale, so prefer `~/.bun/bin/bun run <script>` in fresh shells.
- Common commands:
  - Dev server: `~/.bun/bin/bun run dev` on `http://localhost:8080/`
  - Build: `~/.bun/bin/bun run build` or `~/.bun/bin/bun run build:dev`
  - Lint: `~/.bun/bin/bun run lint`
  - Unit tests: `~/.bun/bin/bun run test`
- This repository is a Vite + React + TypeScript single-page app backed by hosted Supabase. There is no local database or backend service to boot before working on frontend flows.
- Core app structure:
  - Routes: `src/App.tsx`
  - Intake funnel: `src/SpryApp.jsx`
  - Intake data: `src/data/careCatalog.ts`
  - Intake flow logic: `src/lib/intakeFlow.ts`
  - Checkout handoff: `src/pages/CashPayCheckout.tsx`
  - Ops UI: `src/pages/ops/`
- Ops API work must preserve staff auth requirements in `api/_lib/staffAuth.ts`; `/ops?demo=1` is the demo entrypoint.
- Keep shared Cursor assets committed under `.cursor/`, but never commit `.cursor/mcp.json` because it is local-only and gitignored.
